# Cleansing Wildfire on Bot2's Island: Bot2 (the land's controller, not the caster) accepts and fetches a Forest, which
# enters tapped, after the Island is destroyed; Bot1 then draws a card. An Ornithopter (a creature) is not a legal target (`!` with a
# positive control: the land is accepted). Hand 7 - Wildfire - 2 lands + the turn-3 draw + the spell's draw = 6.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mountain
Cleansing Wildfire
Mountain x4
Mountain x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Ornithopter
Island x5
Island x2
Forest
Island x9

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#2.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Cleansing Wildfire.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Hand.Cleansing Wildfire.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Island)
Bot2.Accept
Bot2.Search(Forest)

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Cleansing Wildfire
Bot2.Graveyard = Island
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Tapped = true
Bot1.Hand.Count = 6
